[0m    [38;5;230mMade two changes that need an iTerm2 restart:[39m

    [38;5;230m1. Option Key Sends: Normal (0) → Esc+ (1) — this tells iTerm2 to prefix all Option+key combos with ESC, so Alt+Enter will send ESC+Enter naturally[39m
    [38;5;230m2. Removed the Shift+Enter keyboard mapping — without the explicit override to send plain CR, iTerm2's default behavior might pass Shift+Enter through differently[39m

    [38;5;230mRestart iTerm2 and we'll test again. This is a more fundamental change — Esc+ mode changes how the Option key works globally, so it should definitely affect Alt+Enter.[39m
